      "side": 1,
      "message": "NIT: Question about the extension model. currently serialize only properties_t, so extensions can include interface properties but not data exposed through methods. How would a user attach data from an interface that provides its information through methods instead of properties, such as a large record retrieval API? Is the expectation that such data should be exposed as properties, or do we see a need for a more generic extension mechanism in the future?",
      "revId": "61e59855b91caf0c2a31d9f7022ef4ed954b7f79",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43255547_73cf70c9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-05T19:45:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We would only provide extensions for raw data and not data hid indirectly through methods.  Data hid indirectly through methods isn\u0027t actually part of an interface; it is effectively implementation specific.  Even if we had a way to transfer the data there would be no way for phosphor-logging to recreate it, unless it had a unique implementation of every extension (instead of using the bindings).",
      "parentUuid": "53af28af_27295a28",
      "revId": "61e59855b91caf0c2a31d9f7022ef4ed954b7f79",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
